  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Sound-Design Workbench",
    "overview": "Warm paper surfaces and compact, plainly named controls frame a colorful moving canvas. The interface feels quiet and practical: image identities provide recognition while olive and terracotta actions establish playback and recording priority.\n\nThe shipped system uses one bundled sans-serif family, delicate borders, and softly rounded containers. Ceramic tokens and a rounded rectangular garden playfield belong to the simulation; editor surfaces give those materials room to read.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper and fine dividers.",
      "Persistent pastel identities across images and sounds.",
      "Olive playback and terracotta recording controls.",
